    <div class=entry>
        
            
        
            
        
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
                     <div class=section>
                         <div class=sectname>OFFSET</div>
                         <div class=sectbody>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline>0,5</div>
                             
                         </div>
                     </div>
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
                     <div class=section>
                         <div class=sectname>COMMENTS</div>
                         <div class=sectbody>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline>Zero divisors of the form e+f where e and f are units of the Cayley-Dickson algebra with 2^n elements.</div>
                             
                         </div>
                     </div>
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                     
                 
                 
                     <div class=section>
                         <div class=sectname>LINKS</div>
                         <div class=sectbody>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline><a href="/A167654/b167654.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n=0..8.</a></div>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline>Joerg Arndt, <a href="http://www.jjj.de/fxt/#fxtbook">Matters Computational (The Fxtbook)</a> section 39.14.4 &quot;Simple zero-divisors of the sedenions&quot;, p.820-821.</div>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline>Joerg Arndt, <a href="http://www.jjj.de/fxt/demo/arith/#zero-divisors">List</a> of simple zero-divisors of the sedenions.</div>
                             
                         </div>
                     </div>
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
                     <div class=section>
                         <div class=sectname>EXAMPLE</div>
                         <div class=sectbody>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline>There are no zero-divisors for reals (n=0), complex numbers (n==1), quaternions (n=2), and octonions (n=3). For the sedenions there are 42 sums of two units that are zero divisors. For example ( 1 + 10 ) * ( 5 + 14 ) is zero, so (1+10) is a simple zero divisor (writing k for the k-th unit, starting with 0).</div>
                             
                         </div>
                     </div>
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                     
                 
                 
                 
                     <div class=section>
                         <div class=sectname>CROSSREFS</div>
                         <div class=sectbody>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline>Sequence in context: <a href="/A248466" title="Number of length 5+2 0..n arrays with no three consecutive terms having the sum of any two elements equal to twice the third.">A248466</a> <a href="/A233407" title="Number of (n+1)X(6+1) 0..2 arrays with row and column sums nondecreasing, and no adjacent elements equal.">A233407</a> <a href="/A272139" title="Numbers n such that Bernoulli number B_{n} has denominator 1806.">A272139</a> * <a href="/A095266" title="A sequence generated from the Narayana triangle considered as a matrix, or from Pascal's triangle.">A095266</a> <a href="/A232338" title="Number of 4Xn 0..2 arrays with every 0 next to a 1 and every 1 next to a 2 horizontally or antidiagonally, with no adjacent ...">A232338</a> <a href="/A252937" title="Number of nX7 nonnegative integer arrays with upper left 0 and every value within 3 of its king move distance from the upper...">A252937</a></div>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline>Adjacent sequences:  <a href="/A167651" title="Number of reduced words of length n in Coxeter group on 6 generators S_i with relations (S_i)^2 = (S_i S_j)^15 = I.">A167651</a> <a href="/A167652" title="Number of reduced words of length n in Coxeter group on 7 generators S_i with relations (S_i)^2 = (S_i S_j)^15 = I.">A167652</a> <a href="/A167653" title="Number of reduced words of length n in Coxeter group on 8 generators S_i with relations (S_i)^2 = (S_i S_j)^15 = I.">A167653</a> * <a href="/A167655" title="Riordan array (1-u,u) where u=x/(1+x+x^2).">A167655</a> <a href="/A167656" title="Triangle T(n,k), 0&lt;=k&lt;=n, read by rows given by [1,1,2,1,2,1,2,1,2,1,2,...] DELTA [1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,...] where DELTA is the...">A167656</a> <a href="/A167657" title="Product of n-th block of identical consecutive values of A000720.">A167657</a></div>
                             
                         </div>
                     </div>
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
                     <div class=section>
                         <div class=sectname>KEYWORD</div>
                         <div class=sectbody>
                             
                                 <div class=sectline><span title="more terms are needed! please extend this sequence">more</span>,<span title="a sequence of nonnegative numbers">nonn</span></div>
                             
                         </div>
                     </div>
                 
            
        
            
                 
                 
                 
                 
